hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2881","**\nNarrated to us Hārūn ibn Isḥāq al-Hamdānī, narrated to us Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth, on the authority of Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, on the authority of his brother al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās (RA), who said:\n*\I was riding behind the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and he continued to recite the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah. He stoned it with seven pebbles"","" saying 'Allāhu Akbar' with each pebble.\""*\n\nAbū Bakr (RA) said: *\""This narration of ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Shaybānī"","" from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth"","" has a different chapter.\""*"""""
